# Code style

## TypeScript

- Strict mode; avoid `any` unless necessary
- Target ES2022, module ESNext, bundler resolution
- `verbatimModuleSyntax`, `isolatedModules`, JSX `react-jsx`
- Typecheck only via `bun check` (no emit for packages in the usual flow)

## Imports

```typescript
// Workspace packages
import { SomeSchema } from "@involvex/ctrl-s";

// Node built-ins — always node: protocol
import { join } from "node:path";
import { readFile } from "node:fs/promises";
```

## Naming

- Functions / variables: `camelCase`
- Types / components: `PascalCase`
- Prefer existing package file naming; stay consistent within a package

## Boundaries & errors

- Parse external input with Zod from `@involvex/ctrl-s` at the edge
- Do not leak internal errors to clients; log server-side appropriately
- Gateway binds `127.0.0.1` by default; LAN (`0.0.0.0`) needs explicit pairing

## UI (desktop / mobile / web)

- Matrix dark only: `#000000` bg, `#00ff66` accent, containers `#111613`
- Monospace fonts (JetBrains Mono / Fira Code)
- Thin borders, sharp edges — no rounded iOS-style chrome
- Desktop: exclusive panels (one open); Escape closes; keyboard-friendly nav

## Quality commands (Bun-native only)

```bash
bun run validate   # check + lint + format check
bun check
bun lint           # bun lint --fix when fixing
bun run format:write
```

Never introduce ESLint or Prettier as project dependencies.
